1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,300
Two Roads, One Winter

2
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:06,258
Chidi: Ah! Who opened the freezer?

3
00:00:06,358 --> 00:00:14,640
Uncle Emeka: Chidi! You don land? I'm working a double shift. Take the bus, the 125.

4
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,261
Chidi: No wahala, Uncle. Where's the bus stop?
(No problem, Uncle.)

5
00:00:18,361 --> 00:00:19,980
Uncle Emeka: The one wey dey shake.
(The one where everybody is shivering.)

6
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:35,193
Tía Rosa: ¡Mijo! Come, come. In this house, three rules: we work, we eat, and always, always, we call the family.

7
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:26,730
[Tía Rosa's house, Southwest Detroit]

8
00:00:35,293 --> 00:00:37,882
Mateo: Sí, tía. Okay.

9
00:00:37,982 --> 00:00:39,752
Luis: Tomorrow I pick you up at five.

10
00:00:39,852 --> 00:00:41,303
Mateo: Five in the afternoon?

11
00:00:41,403 --> 00:00:44,746
Luis: In the morning, primo. Welcome to Detroit.

12
00:00:44,996 --> 00:00:47,696
Two years earlier

13
00:00:47,846 --> 00:00:48,987
Agent: Where you from?

14
00:00:49,087 --> 00:00:50,131
Mateo: Honduras.

15
00:00:50,231 --> 00:00:54,291
Man in cell: Welcome to la hielera, brother. The icebox.

16
00:00:54,541 --> 00:00:57,241
Notice to Appear: a court date in a city he has never heard of

17
00:00:57,541 --> 00:01:00,241
Interstate 10, heading east

18
00:01:00,541 --> 00:01:03,241
Border Patrol checkpoint, Sierra Blanca, Texas

19
00:01:07,541 --> 00:01:10,241
Houston. Two years of drywall.

20
00:01:10,391 --> 00:01:13,583
Luis: Primo, come to Detroit. There is work.

21
00:01:13,683 --> 00:01:15,066
Mateo: The icebox again.

22
00:01:15,216 --> 00:01:18,316
[A store in Southfield, that same week]

23
00:01:21,666 --> 00:01:24,049
Mr. Daniels: Sir. Can I help you find something?

24
00:01:24,149 --> 00:01:35,995
Chidi: Uncle! Good afternoon, sir. How is your family? Please, this coat. $109. What is your last price?

25
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:37,477
Mr. Daniels: My... last price?

26
00:01:37,577 --> 00:01:43,879
Chidi: In Lagos we talk. You say a price, I say a price, we meet in the middle like brothers.

27
00:01:43,979 --> 00:01:49,008
Mr. Daniels: Brother, the price is on the sticker. And I'm not the cashier. I'm security.

28
00:01:49,108 --> 00:01:51,748
Chidi: Ah. So you were watching me.

29
00:01:51,848 --> 00:01:54,536
Mr. Daniels: You've been in here two hours in a bedsheet.

30
00:01:54,636 --> 00:01:58,280
Chidi: It is a wrapper. And it is the warmest thing I own.

31
00:01:58,380 --> 00:01:59,404
Mr. Daniels: First winter?

32
00:01:59,504 --> 00:02:00,588
Chidi: First week.

33
00:02:00,688 --> 00:02:08,007
Mr. Daniels: Grace Fellowship, on the corner by the gas station. Saturday coat drive. Tell Sister Gloria that Daniels sent you.

34
00:02:08,107 --> 00:02:09,947
Chidi: God bless you, Uncle.

35
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:12,954
Mr. Daniels: And quit calling me Uncle. I'm thirty-one.

36
00:02:13,104 --> 00:02:16,004
[Mateo's first roofing job]

37
00:02:16,054 --> 00:02:23,766
Boss: Okay, listen. Take off the old shingles on the back. And don't step on the soft spot, or you fall through my roof.

38
00:02:23,866 --> 00:02:25,432
Mateo: Okay, boss.

39
00:02:25,532 --> 00:02:27,104
Mateo: Primo... what he say?

40
00:02:27,204 --> 00:02:30,528
Luis: Don't step in the hole. The rest, I show you.

41
00:02:32,628 --> 00:02:34,346
Mateo: Tía, they pay me less.

42
00:02:34,446 --> 00:02:42,759
Tía Rosa: No fighting, mijo. With respect. Write your hours on paper, and ask for it in writing.

43
00:02:42,859 --> 00:02:44,301
Boss: Who taught you to do that?

44
00:02:44,401 --> 00:02:45,441
Mateo: My tía.

45
00:02:45,541 --> 00:02:47,811
Boss: Tell your tía she should run payroll.

46
00:02:47,961 --> 00:02:50,861
[Saturday: the church coat drive]

47
00:02:50,911 --> 00:02:54,581
Chidi: Good morning, Auntie. Daniels sent me.

48
00:02:54,681 --> 00:02:58,007
Sister Gloria: Then you're in the right place. What size are you, baby?

49
00:02:58,107 --> 00:03:01,414
Chidi: Auntie, if I take two, what is the discount?

50
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:02,653
Sister Gloria: They're free.

51
00:03:02,753 --> 00:03:04,745
Chidi: Then the discount is very good.

52
00:03:04,845 --> 00:03:11,483
Mateo: It's free, hermano. Free! Take the big one. The wind here... ¡fuuu!

53
00:03:11,583 --> 00:03:12,893
Chidi: You are also new?

54
00:03:12,993 --> 00:03:15,166
Mateo: One month. You?

55
00:03:15,266 --> 00:03:19,149
Chidi: One week. I am already a professional at shaking.

56
00:03:19,249 --> 00:03:20,163
Mateo: ¡Genial!
(Great!)

57
00:03:20,263 --> 00:03:22,871
Chidi: Genial? What is genial?

58
00:03:22,971 --> 00:03:25,675
Mateo: Like... very good. Cool.

59
00:03:25,775 --> 00:03:27,848
Chidi: In Lagos we say "e choke."
(It's amazing.)

60
00:03:27,948 --> 00:03:28,829
Mateo: ¿E choke?

61
00:03:28,929 --> 00:03:29,876
Chidi: E choke!

62
00:03:29,976 --> 00:03:30,851
Chidi: (muffled) Genial.

63
00:03:30,951 --> 00:03:37,861
Uncle Emeka: Chidi, relax. Detroit na sanctuary city. Nobody go disturb you.
(Detroit is a sanctuary city. Nobody will bother you.)

64
00:03:31,001 --> 00:03:34,101
[Church dinner, after the coat drive]

65
00:03:37,961 --> 00:03:43,676
Luis: No, no, no. Detroit is not sanctuary. It's a "welcoming city."

66
00:03:43,776 --> 00:03:45,258
Chidi: What is the difference?

67
00:03:45,358 --> 00:03:51,332
Luis: Welcoming means the city police aren't supposed to ask your papers. Sanctuary means... something more.

68
00:03:51,432 --> 00:03:56,563
Tía Rosa: And ICE is federal. They don't ask the city permission for nothing.

69
00:03:56,663 --> 00:03:58,084
Uncle Emeka: So it's welcoming...

70
00:03:58,184 --> 00:03:59,608
Tía Rosa: ...pero con chaqueta.
(...but bring a jacket.)

71
00:03:59,708 --> 00:04:03,202
Tía Rosa: Keep this in your wallet. Always.

72
00:04:03,302 --> 00:04:18,497
Chidi: I came on a visitor visa. My I-94 says how long I can stay. So before it ran out, I filed my I-589, the asylum form. Now I wait months before they even let me file the I-765 for a work permit.

73
00:04:03,352 --> 00:04:06,452
[Uncle Emeka's apartment]

74
00:04:18,597 --> 00:04:24,921
Chidi: In Nigeria I taught 40 children algebra. Here I am not allowed to work, so I count snowflakes.

75
00:04:29,021 --> 00:04:30,154
Sister Gloria: You eat today?

76
00:04:29,071 --> 00:04:30,204
[The church food pantry]

77
00:04:30,254 --> 00:04:32,068
Chidi: I am fine, Auntie.

78
00:04:32,168 --> 00:04:39,385
Sister Gloria: That's not what I asked. Here. Ask for Help. Type what you need. Real people answer.

79
00:04:44,485 --> 00:04:48,614
Chidi: A maths tutor. Auntie, I was born for this.

80
00:04:48,714 --> 00:04:54,368
Mateo: They took Don Beto. At his check-in. He go like always, and he don't come out.

81
00:04:48,764 --> 00:04:51,864
[Tía Rosa's house]

82
00:04:54,468 --> 00:04:57,586
Tía Rosa: First we pray. Then we call.

83
00:05:00,686 --> 00:05:08,023
Mateo: Chidi. Beto's kids, they have math homework. Their papa is... not home. You can help?

84
00:05:08,123 --> 00:05:12,009
Chidi: I am coming. Tell them to sharpen their pencils.

85
00:05:16,609 --> 00:05:19,475
Chidi: Auntie, what if I go in and I don't come out?

86
00:05:16,659 --> 00:05:19,525
[Immigration court]

87
00:05:19,575 --> 00:05:24,701
Sister Gloria: Then I'll be sitting right here, and I'll make the calls. But today, we go in.

88
00:05:24,801 --> 00:05:27,301
Chidi: The judge says come back in fourteen months.

89
00:05:27,401 --> 00:05:30,280
Sister Gloria: That's good news. You're still here.

90
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:33,360
Chidi: In Nigeria, fourteen months is a sentence.

91
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:37,872
Sister Gloria: Here it's a calendar. Come on, the kids are waiting on their tutor.

92
00:05:38,122 --> 00:05:40,822
Poco a poco (Little by little)

93
00:05:43,972 --> 00:05:45,649
Luis: Today, you are the boss.

94
00:05:45,899 --> 00:05:49,099
Mr. Chidi's Maths Club

95
00:05:49,249 --> 00:05:51,547
Chidi: Uncle! It came!

96
00:05:51,647 --> 00:05:53,707
Mail carrier: Everybody's your uncle, huh?

97
00:05:53,957 --> 00:05:56,157
Next November

98
00:05:56,307 --> 00:05:58,913
Chidi: Welcome. First winter?

99
00:05:59,013 --> 00:06:06,059
Chidi: No wahala. Take this one, and this one. Free. No discount needed.
(No problem.)

100
00:06:06,159 --> 00:06:09,772
Mateo: ¿Qué tal, profe? How you doing, teacher?

101
00:06:09,872 --> 00:06:12,933
Chidi: E choke, my brother. And you?

102
00:06:13,033 --> 00:06:13,946
Mateo: ¡Genial!
(Great!)

103
00:06:16,696 --> 00:06:23,196
"I was a stranger, and ye took me in." Matthew 25:35

